FliperOS: low dotclocks on nouveau analog outputs (VGA, DVI-I/DVI-A)

nouveau_connector_mode_valid() rejects every mode under 25 MHz, so the
video=640x480iS boot mode of the 15 kHz patch and the user modes of patch 06
(Switchres drmkms) never reach the DAC. Batocera community reports show
GeForce 8400 GS and Quadro K600 on nouveau running at dotclock_min 0. Only the analog encoder changes: TMDS, DP and LVDS
keep their limits. fliperos-setup still confirms it per card with a grid
test before using native modes.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c
@@ -1096,6 +1096,9 @@
 		max_clock = get_tmds_link_bandwidth(connector);
 		break;
 	case DCB_OUTPUT_ANALOG:
+		/* 15 kHz CRTs need dotclocks of 6-15 MHz. Whether the PLL of
+		 * a given card reaches them is tested by fliperos-setup. */
+		min_clock = 0;
 		max_clock = nv_encoder->dcb->crtconf.maxfreq;
 		if (!max_clock)
 			max_clock = 350000;
